WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.530
Build multiplication facts from known facts. For example, 6 times 7 equals 5 times 7

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:09.907
plus 7, so 35 plus 7 equals 42.

00:00:10.783 --> 00:00:18.296
Use the known fact 8 times 5 equals 40 to find 9 times 5. The answer is 45. Add one

00:00:18.296 --> 00:00:21.301
group of 5: 40 plus 5 equals 45.

00:00:22.117 --> 00:00:27.480
A learner during a library project knows 4 times 5 equals 20. How can they calculate

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.503
5 times 5 using one more group? Pause the video and think.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:38.169
A learner during a library project knows 4 times 5 equals 20. How can they calculate

00:00:38.169 --> 00:00:45.060
5 times 5 using one more group? The answer is 25. Add one group of 5: 20 plus 5

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:45.785
equals 25.
